; Journal.query() under --group-by-cumulative returns each group's own
; postings, as `reg --group-by-cumulative` reports them: with -r the
; Expenses:Utilities group holds the Grocer's Expenses:Food and
; Assets:Checking postings, as without --group-by-cumulative, -V (no
; prices here) changes none of them, and -S sorts each group's postings
; afresh.  -P results hold the payee subtotals, which used to be freed
; while the result (and, under --group-by-cumulative, the next group)
; still pointed at them.

2012/01/15 Electric Company
    Expenses:Utilities          $50.00
    Assets:Checking

2012/02/03 Grocer
    Expenses:Food               $20.00
    Expenses:Utilities           $5.00
    Assets:Checking

2012/02/15 Electric Company
    Expenses:Utilities          $55.00
    Assets:Checking

2012/02/20 Electric Company
    Expenses:Utilities          10 EUR
    Assets:Checking

test python test/regress/py-query-group-by-cumulative.py
--group-by account -r Expenses: 7 posts, 7 amounts
  2012-02-03 Grocer Expenses:Utilities $5.00
